The protocol object reference uses the non-null assertion operator (!) but the null check is performed just before. While this is safe, consider refactoring to avoid the assertion:

```typescript
if (protocol) {
    const discoveryRoute = protocol.getDiscovery();
    this.app.get('/api/v1', (c) => c.json(discoveryRoute));
}
```

This makes the code clearer and avoids the need for TypeScript's non-null assertion.
```suggestion
            this.app.get('/api/v1', (c) => c.json(protocol.getDiscovery()));
```

The server shutdown in the destroy method may not work correctly. The Hono serve function may not return an object with a close method, and even if it does, calling close() doesn't wait for the server to actually stop (no await).

Consider:
1. Checking the actual return type from serve() in the Hono library
2. If a close method exists, awaiting it or wrapping it in a promise if it's callback-based
3. Adding error handling for the close operation
4. Ensuring resources are properly cleaned up even if close fails
```suggestion
        const server = this.server as
            | undefined
            | {
                  close?: ((callback: (err?: Error) => void) => void | unknown) | (() => void | Promise<void>);
              };

        if (server && typeof server.close === 'function') {
            try {
                // Support Node-style callback-based close (e.g., http.Server.close(cb))
                if (server.close.length > 0) {
                    await new Promise<void>((resolve, reject) => {
                        (server.close as (cb: (err?: Error) => void) => void)((err?: Error) => {
                            if (err) {
                                reject(err);
                            } else {
                                resolve();
                            }
                        });
                    });
                } else {
                    // Support promise-returning or synchronous close()
                    const result = (server.close as () => void | Promise<void>)();
                    if (result instanceof Promise) {
                        await result;
                    }
                }
                console.log('[HonoServerPlugin] Server stopped');
            } catch (error) {
                console.error('[HonoServerPlugin] Error while stopping server', error);
            }
```
